<title>FRANCE: Syrian durum wheat mostly destined to Libya-trader.</title>
<headline>Syrian durum wheat mostly destined to Libya-trader.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria's recent sale of 40,000 tonnes of durum wheat is mostly destined to Libya, European grain exporters said on Monday.</p>
<p>Syria's General Establishment for Cereal Processing and Trade has said it sold 40,000 tonnes of hard amber durum wheat at $195 per tonne to a German company.</p>
<p>Exporters said Libya bought at the end of last week between 20,000 and 40,000 tonnes of Syrian barley for shipment in March.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
